WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
- Let's finish up with one last story,

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.670
I hope you're gonna love as much as I do.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.221
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:05.221 --> 00:00:06.621
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.621 --> 00:00:08.420
(crowd cheering)

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.920
This year's March Madness

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.560
has already given us all
its usual narratives,

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.970
the unexpected defeats, mm-hmm,

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.670
narrow victories, the
Cinderella storyline,

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.460
but there's one moment from the sidelines

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.830
that you may have missed,

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.420
halfway through the Indiana
University St. Mary's

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.570
round one game.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.810
The ball got jammed between the backboard

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.240
and the shot clock.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.750
Players tried jumping
for it, no such luck.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.960
They tried dislodging it
with a mop, it did not work.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.830
So, check out how it did work.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.113
- [Announcer] Well, maybe he's
gotta go on Verns shoulders.

00:00:37.113 --> 00:00:38.520
(crowd jeering)

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.800
- [Announcer two] We
got Toss holding Fiffer,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.776
that's, Kelly is not tall enough.

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:43.980
(crowd jeering)

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.095
- [Announcer] Major
issues here in Portland.

00:00:46.095 --> 00:00:48.090
(crowd jeering)

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.340
- [Announcer two] Why don't
we get a new ball, why?

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:53.040
Why don't the cheerleaders
they're used to going up high?

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:53.997
Let's get a--

00:00:53.997 --> 00:00:54.830
Yes!

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.620
Get the cheerleader up.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:57.602
Get her up there.

00:00:57.602 --> 00:00:59.753
(crowd cheering) This is how you do it.

00:00:59.753 --> 00:01:02.343
(crowd cheering)

00:01:02.343 --> 00:01:03.300
Give her the mop.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.517
Now she's got it.

00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:05.700
(crowd cheering)

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.033
Oh, what a play?

00:01:08.215 --> 00:01:10.708
The cheerleader saves the day.

00:01:10.708 --> 00:01:13.310
(crowd cheering)

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.570
- I love this story for so many reasons.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.960
One being like, were there no
other basketballs to be found?

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.350
Like that's my favorite.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:22.730
They were like, "It's the only ball

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.090
we could have possibly used."

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.850
We have those nimble cheerleaders

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.070
on the line now watching

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:29.720
on WTHR Indianapolis at 11:00 AM.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.231
Say hi to Cassidy and Nathan.

00:01:32.231 --> 00:01:33.390
(audience applauding)

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.763
What's up y'all?

00:01:34.763 --> 00:01:36.043
(audience applauding)

00:01:36.043 --> 00:01:38.100
So all these, all these big old dudes

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.310
out there try to get this ball.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.070
So what were you thinking
when the ball got stuck?

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.200
Did you know you were gonna do that?

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.530
- I just remember thinking
like the crowd is booing.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.740
Everyone is booing at the players

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.870
for not being able to get
it down and the refs but--

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:53.980
- Yeah, we were watching

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.130
and the players were jumping
up trying to grab it.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.200
It was too high.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.140
And then we had the referee get

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.460
on the chair and that clearly
wasn't working as well.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.640
So now the crowd's booing even louder.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:09.130
And so I hear our coach
from the sidelines tell us

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:10.140
that we need to put a stunt up.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.710
We need to get somebody up in the air,

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:12.600
and Cass was ready to go.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.700
So I grabbed her and we made it happen.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.533
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:16.688
(audience applauding)

00:02:16.688 --> 00:02:17.521
So--

00:02:17.521 --> 00:02:18.841
(audience applauding)

00:02:18.841 --> 00:02:19.910
Did you think you were gonna

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:20.980
be able to pull it up, Cassy?

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.270
'Cause even when you
went up the first time

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:24.477
before he lifted his arms, it
still looked like it was like,

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.060
"Oh, I'm gonna be too short for this."

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.890
- I was a little nervous,
but I had to get underneath

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.160
the bar, 'cause I was a little too tall,

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:35.360
surprisingly, and I had to
bend down and shift my weight

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.120
which can be a little hard to
hold, but we pulled it off.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.300
- Yeah, you did.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.664
(audience applauding)

00:02:41.664 --> 00:02:43.247
Go ahead, go ahead.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.320
- I was super nervous

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.750
because I thought that was
the worst possible moment

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:48.690
to drop a stunt.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.640
If I was gonna drop one in
front of, you know, national TV.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:53.553
- Cause everyone's watching.

00:02:53.553 --> 00:02:55.417
- But we got it up.

00:02:55.417 --> 00:02:56.530
Exactly.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:59.640
And so we got the stunt up
and we got it all figured out

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.950
but unfortunately our team lost,

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.320
but it was like such a great
experience just to be there

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.080
with our program and with our school.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.420
And it was just an awesome moment.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.180
- Aaw, it was so cool.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.590
Thank you guys so much.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:13.573
Thank you Cassy and Nathan.
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:13.573 --> 00:03:15.056
(crowd applauding)

00:03:15.056 --> 00:03:16.100
(ring)

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:18.650
And that's not all our season
long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.290
makers of G2, the go to pen
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.700
want to honor ultimate
overachievers just like y'all.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.380
So they're gonna be writing you a cheque

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.310
for a thousand dollars.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.440
That's 500 bucks each.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.301
How does that sound?

00:03:28.301 --> 00:03:31.512
(audience applauding)

00:03:31.512 --> 00:03:32.470
- Thank you so much.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:33.630
(audience applauding)

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.880
- It was worth the stunt.

